 ### Adaptive Number of Updates
 An adaptive system to adjust the number of opacity map updates ($k$) per frame based on performance history to balance rendering speed and occlusion detection overhead [S1].
-*   **Polling:** Every $n$-th frame (e.g., $n=10$), poll performance using the number in range $[k-h_w, k+h_w]$ that has not been updated for the longest. Increment age of all slots by 1 except the polled one [S1].
-*   **Update $k$:** When all slots are valid, pick the slot with best performance as the new center. Change $k$ to this new center and shift performance statistics accordingly [S1].
+*   **Polling:** Every $n$-th frame (e.g., $n=10$), poll performance using the number in range $[k-h_w, k+h_w]$ that has not been updated for the longest [S1]. Increment age of all slots by 1 except the polled one [S1].
+*   **Update $k$:** When all slots are valid, pick the slot with best performance as the new center [S1]. Change $k$ to this new center and shift performance statistics accordingly [S1].
 *   **Performance function:** $p = v - c \cdot k$, where $v$ is the percentage of voxels culled and clipped, $k$ is the actual number of map updates, and $c$ is a constant (0.02 for tested datasets) [S1].
 *   **Parameter:** $k$: Initial empirically determined number of map updates (typically 9) [S1].
